5
00:00:16,698 --> 00:00:19,790
NASA and ISRO's NISAR radar sees it.

6
00:00:20,030 --> 00:00:24,146
SARtale turns every NISAR pass into lake water area,

7
00:00:24,186 --> 00:00:27,370
compared with each lake's normal range.

8
00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:33,630
An officer opens Lake Watch, thirty-nine lakes so far, and picks Passu.

9
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:36,940
Its page shows the radar water and its history.

10
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:40,623
All three flagged lakes began with a NISAR processing

11
00:00:40,663 --> 00:00:43,220
update, so none is a confirmed change.

12
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:48,769
Officers can check imagery, contact NDMA or PDMA, or print a brief.

13
00:00:48,809 --> 00:00:51,040
Screening, not a warning.

14
